The cell 'span differing from the document by case / value absent from the span' specifies that the span is present in the document but differs in case, and the value is not contained within that span. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [a84bcb8e1134b8b4]. Because 'no relaxation' is specified for the span-in-document check, a span that differs from the document by case is not considered to occur in the document, implying a verdict of SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT. In the rewritten text, I change the span to match the document character for character. The rule then implies a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN, because the value remains absent from the span. Thus, the verdict moves from SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT to VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN.